<type>(<scope>): <description> (#<issue>)

# Optional body: explain what changed and why.
#
# Format:
#   <type>(<scope>): <description> (#<issue>)
#
# Types:
#   feat      New features
#   fix       Bug fixes
#   refactor  Internal changes without behavioral changes
#   test      Adding or modifying tests
#   docs      Documentation changes
#   build     Build system and dependency changes
#   ci        CI/CD configuration changes
#   perf      Performance improvements
#   chore     Other maintenance tasks
#
# Subject rules:
#   - Write in English and use the imperative mood.
#   - Start the description with a lowercase letter.
#   - Do not end the subject with a period.
#   - Keep the subject within 72 characters whenever practical.
#   - Be specific; avoid descriptions such as "update files" or "fix bug".
#   - Scope is optional; use it only when it identifies a useful component.
#   - Include (#<issue>) when a corresponding GitHub Issue exists.
#
# Body rules:
#   - Separate the body from the subject with a blank line.
#   - Explain what changed and why, not obvious implementation details.
#   - Wrap body lines at 72 characters whenever practical.
#
# Examples:
#   fix(request): correct async HTTP argument forwarding (#12)
#   docs: improve installation instructions
#
# Breaking changes:
#   Use <type>(<scope>)!: ... or add a BREAKING CHANGE: footer.
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md for the complete commit rules.
